+# Contract: HTML Export Format
+
+**Feature**: `002-import-html-export` | **Date**: 2026-11-14
+
+`export` gains a third format. The CSV and JSON formats are unchanged and remain specified by
+[001/contracts/output-formats.md](../../001-bookmark-cli-manager/contracts/output-formats.md);
+their bytes MUST stay identical to what the previous version wrote (FR-045).
+
+## Invocation
+
+```text
+python -m bookmarks [--db PATH] export --format {csv,json,html}
+```
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| stdout on success | the whole collection as one HTML page, bookmarks in ascending id order (FR-039) |
+| Exit 0 | page written, including for an empty store (FR-039, FR-043) |
+| Exit 1 | `--format` omitted or any value other than `csv`, `json`, `html`; stderr names the problem (FR-044) |
+| Side effects | read-only; the store is opened (and created if absent) but never modified |
+
+Order is the same order as `list`, `export --format csv` and `export --format json`: ascending id
+(FR-039). `import --format html` does not exist — HTML is export-only.
+
+## Page bytes
+
+Nine fixed lines plus one line per bookmark, each line terminated by `\n`, including the last
+(FR-040). For a store holding bookmark 1 (`https://docs.python.org`, `Python docs`, tags
+`docs,python`) and bookmark 2 (`https://example.com`, `Example`, no tags), stdout is **exactly**:
+
+```html
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html>
+<head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Bookmarks</title></head>
+<body>
+<ul>
+<li><a href="https://docs.python.org">Python docs</a> <small>docs,python</small></li>
+<li><a href="https://example.com">Example</a> <small></small></li>
+</ul>
+</body>
+</html>
+```
+
+Fixed parts, in order (FR-040):
+
+| Line | Content |
+|------|---------|
+| 1 | `<!DOCTYPE html>` |
+| 2 | `<html>` |
+| 3 | `<head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Bookmarks</title></head>` |
+| 4 | `<body>` |
+| 5 | `<ul>` |
+| 6…5+N | one bookmark item each (below) |
+| 6+N | `</ul>` |
+| 7+N | `</body>` |
+| 8+N | `</html>` |
+
+The page is minimal by decision (spec Assumptions): no CSS, no generation timestamp, no bookmark
+count, no ids in the markup, no `lang` attribute, no blank lines, no indentation.
+
+## Bookmark item
+
+Each bookmark is **exactly one line** (FR-041):
+
+```text
+<li><a href="URL">TITLE</a> <small>TAGS</small></li>
+```
+
+| Placeholder | Value | Notes |
+|-------------|-------|-------|
+| `URL` | the bookmark's `url`, HTML-escaped | never percent-encoded or rewritten |
+| `TITLE` | the bookmark's `title`, HTML-escaped | an empty title gives `<a href="…"></a>` |
+| `TAGS` | the bookmark's tags joined by commas in alphabetical order, HTML-escaped | no tags → `<small></small>` |
+
+There is exactly one space between `</a>` and `<small>`, and no other whitespace inside the line.
+Because tags are stored already normalised and alphabetical (FR-011), `TAGS` is the stored `tags`
+string as-is.
+
+## Escaping (FR-042)
+
+Exactly four characters are replaced, wherever they occur in a URL, a title or a tag:
+
+| Character | Emitted as |
+|-----------|-----------|
+| `&` | `&amp;` |
+| `<` | `&lt;` |
+| `>` | `&gt;` |
+| `"` | `&quot;` |
+
+Every other character is emitted **verbatim**, including the apostrophe `'` and all non-ASCII
+text, which the `<head>`'s UTF-8 declaration makes well defined (FR-042, SC-012, see
+[research.md D16](../research.md#d16-html-escaping-covers-exactly----and----not-the-apostrophe)).
+
+Example — a bookmark with url `https://example.com/?a=1&b=2`, title `Tom's "A&B" <notes>`, tags
+`a&b,c<d`:
+
+```html
+<li><a href="https://example.com/?a=1&amp;b=2">Tom's &quot;A&amp;B&quot; &lt;notes&gt;</a> <small>a&amp;b,c&lt;d</small></li>
+```
+
+A browser renders the stored text, and the page stays well-formed.
+
+## Empty store (FR-043)
+
+The skeleton prints unchanged with no items between `<ul>` and `</ul>`, exit status 0:
+
+```html
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html>
+<head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Bookmarks</title></head>
+<body>
+<ul>
+</ul>
+</body>
+</html>
+```
+
+## Encoding
+
+stdout is UTF-8 regardless of locale, as for every other command
+([001/research.md D7](../../001-bookmark-cli-manager/research.md)), which is what the declared
+charset promises a browser (FR-042, SC-012).
