+# Contract: The `import` Command and Its Input Formats
+
+**Feature**: `002-import-html-export` | **Date**: 2026-11-14
+
+This file fixes the sixth command's surface and the exact shape of the files it accepts. The five
+existing commands are unchanged and remain specified by
+[001/contracts/cli.md](../../001-bookmark-cli-manager/contracts/cli.md); the formats `export`
+writes are specified by
+[001/contracts/output-formats.md](../../001-bookmark-cli-manager/contracts/output-formats.md) and
+are the formats this command reads.
+
+## Invocation
+
+```text
+python -m bookmarks [--db PATH] import FILE --format {csv,json}
+```
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| Arguments | `FILE` (positional, required): path to the file to read. `--format` (required): `csv` or `json` |
+| `--db PATH` | the global option, before the command, exactly as for every other command; omitted → `bookmarks.db` in the current directory; created if absent (FR-002, FR-003) |
+| stdout on success | exactly `imported N\n`, where N is the number of bookmarks added — **and nothing else** (FR-026) |
+| stdout on failure | **empty** (FR-034, FR-035, SC-011) |
+| Exit 0 | every bookmark in the file was added, in file order, with ids assigned by the store (FR-025, FR-026); N may be 0 (FR-038) |
+| Exit 2 | the file was refused — unreadable, not UTF-8, not the documented shape, or carrying a URL `add` would reject. Nothing added; the store is byte-identical and the highest id ever used is unchanged (FR-034…FR-037) |
+| Exit 1 | usage error (`--format` missing or not `csv`/`json`, `FILE` missing, unknown option), or the store could not be opened or created (FR-047) |
+| Side effects | reads `FILE`; appends rows to the store. Never writes to `FILE`; never writes anywhere else; no network access |
+
+`import --format html` does not exist: `html` is an export-only format, so `--format html` here is
+a usage error (exit 1), not a rejected file.
+
+## Semantics
+
+1. Each bookmark in the file is added **exactly as `add` would add it** (FR-032): the URL prefix
+   rule (FR-009), the title stored verbatim (FR-010, FR-023), the tag rules (FR-011, FR-028), ids
+   from the store and never reused (FR-008).
+2. Any `id` in the file has **no effect** (FR-033). New ids continue after the highest id ever
+   used in that store, so importing into a store that already holds ids 1–2 yields 3, 4, ….
+3. Bookmarks are added in **file order** (FR-025), so ids reflect the order the file lists them.
+4. There is **no deduplication** (spec Assumptions): importing the same file twice yields two
+   independent copies of every bookmark with distinct ids.
+5. An import is **all or nothing** (FR-037): either every bookmark in the file is added, or none
+   is and the exit status is 2. The user never has to determine how far it got.
+
+## CSV input (`--format csv`)
+
+```text
+id,url,title,tags
+1,https://docs.python.org,Python docs,"docs,python"
+2,https://example.com,Example,
+```
+
+- **Line 1 MUST be exactly the header `id,url,title,tags`** — the header
+  `export --format csv` writes (FR-027). Compared after CSV parsing, so `id, url, title, tags`
+  (with spaces) is **rejected**; a CRLF line ending is accepted.
+- Every following row is one bookmark with **exactly four fields** in order: ignored id, URL,
+  title, tags (FR-027). More or fewer fields → rejected (FR-035).
+- Standard CSV quoting is honoured — a quoted field may contain commas, doubled quotes (`""` for
+  one `"`) and line breaks — so **any file `export --format csv` writes reads back as the same
+  field values** (FR-029).
+- The `tags` field is a comma-separated tag list read by the `add --tags` rules: trimmed, empties
+  dropped, duplicates kept once, stored alphabetically (FR-028). An empty field → no tags.
+- A header row alone → `imported 0`, exit 0 (FR-038).
+- An empty file (no header at all) → rejected, exit 2 (FR-035).
+- A blank line between rows parses as a zero-field row → rejected. A single trailing newline after
+  the last row is normal and accepted.
+
+## JSON input (`--format json`)
+
+```json
+[
+  {"url": "https://docs.python.org", "title": "Python docs", "tags": ["docs", "python"]},
+  {"url": "https://example.com", "title": "Example", "tags": []}
+]
+```
+
+- The top level MUST be an **array**; each element MUST be an **object** carrying `url` (string),
+  `title` (string) and `tags` (array of strings) (FR-030).
+- `id` and **any other unrecognised key are ignored**, so the output of `export --format json` —
+  which carries `id` — imports unchanged, as does a file from a later version of the tool
+  (FR-031).
+- `tags` entries are read by the `add --tags` rules: trimmed, empties dropped, duplicates kept
+  once, stored alphabetically (FR-028, FR-032). `[]` → no tags.
+- `[]` → `imported 0`, exit 0 (FR-038).
+- Rejected (exit 2, FR-030/FR-035): a top level that is not an array (an object, number, string,
+  `null`); an element that is not an object; a missing `url`, `title` or `tags`; a `url` or
+  `title` that is not a string; a `tags` value that is not an array or that holds a non-string
+  entry.
+
+## Diagnostics (stderr)
+
+Every failure writes at least one line naming what was wrong, and nothing to stdout. Message
+shapes (the wording is informative, the presence of the named value is the contract — SC-011):
+
+| Condition | Status | stderr names |
+|-----------|--------|--------------|
+| File missing / not readable / is a directory | 2 | the path and the OS error |
+| File is not valid UTF-8 | 2 | the path and the decoding problem |
+| CSV header wrong, or file empty | 2 | the required header and what was found |
+| CSV row with the wrong field count | 2 | the row number and the count found |
+| Malformed CSV | 2 | the parse problem |
+| Malformed JSON | 2 | the parse problem with line and column |
+| JSON top level not an array | 2 | the type found |
+| JSON element ill-shaped | 2 | the element's zero-based index and the key at fault |
+| URL rejected by the prefix rule | 2 | the offending URL and the expected `http://`/`https://` prefixes |
+| Store cannot be opened or created | 1 | the store path and the underlying error |
+| Usage error | 1 | the argparse message (`python -m bookmarks: error: …`) |
+
+No traceback is ever printed, and no partial import is ever left behind (SC-010, SC-011).
+
+## Exit statuses, whole tool
+
+Unchanged from [001/contracts/cli.md](../../001-bookmark-cli-manager/contracts/cli.md) except
+that 2 now covers a second refused input (FR-047):
+
+| Status | Meaning |
+|--------|---------|
+| 0 | the requested work completed |
+| 1 | usage error (unknown command or option, missing or malformed argument, unsupported format) or the store could not be opened, created or read |
+| 2 | an input value was refused: `add` rejected the URL's prefix (FR-009), **or `import` rejected the file** (FR-034…FR-036) |
+| 3 | `delete` was given an id that is not in the store (FR-018) |
